@copilot Apply one scoped Copilot-review correction directly to this existing PR, preserving the completed gRPC request-header migration and unconditional current RPC emission. Do not create another PR.

Copilot review 5692486944 correctly identifies a stale migration target in CHANGELOG.md. The existing Unreleased gRPC entry around lines 260-263 removes otel.instrumentation.grpc.capture-metadata.client.request and otel.instrumentation.grpc.capture-metadata.server.request, but still tells users to use otel.instrumentation.grpc.client.request-metadata.included and otel.instrumentation.grpc.server.request-metadata.included. GrpcConfig now reads request_headers, so following that advice no longer enables capture. Change those two replacement properties to otel.instrumentation.grpc.client.request-headers.included and otel.instrumentation.grpc.server.request-headers.included.

Limit this follow-up to that existing Unreleased migration correction. Keep the existing API/configuration migration entries, do not edit released changelog history, do not change production code or tests, and do not include the repository-wide documentation cleanup the user is handling separately. Preserve the PR's draft state. Use the repository's existing targeted Markdown validation if applicable; no Java build is needed for this documentation-only correction.
